==Icelandic==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|is|non|guð}}, from {{der|is|gem-pro|*gudą}}.

The {{IPAchar|/v/}} present in the pronunciation is a remnant of a 16th century sound change in Northwestern Iceland where a {{IPAchar|/v/}} was inserted in words beginning with {{IPAchar|/k/}} or {{IPAchar|/ɡ/}} followed by {{IPAchar|/u/}} or {{IPAchar|/o/}}. This pronunciation eventually disappeared but was preserved in the word ''guð'' (and its derivations) and subsequently spread to the rest of the country.<ref>Veturliði Óskarsson (2001). [http://ait.arnastofnun.is/grein.php?id=703 ”Íslensk málsaga”]. ''Alfræði íslenskrar tungu''. Reykjavík: Lýðveldissjóður og Námsgagnastonun.</ref>

